realloc(NULL, 100) is malloc(100) ok
realloc(NULL, 0) is malloc(0) ok
realloc grows, keeping the contents ok
the grown block is writable ok
realloc moves, freeing the old block ok
realloc moves again, keeping the contents ok
realloc to the same size stays ok
realloc shrinks in place, keeping the contents ok
shrinking frees the rest ok
realloc(p, 0) keeps a unique block ok
realloc(p, 65535) fails with ENOMEM ok
failing keeps the old block ok
realloc fails with ENOMEM when the heap is full ok
failing keeps the old block ok
realloc works after free, keeping the contents ok
